  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining and securing tropical forests</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome: By 2028, global and domestic commodity and financial market actors operating in Brazil, China and Colombia adopt and enforce deforestation &#x2013; and conversion free (DCF) standards.

Outcome indicators: 
Number and type of policies influenced by partner&apos;s work (Core Indicator 1)
Number of national, sub-national, or local traceability systems for key forest-risk commodities that have become operational and effective
Number of national and international cooperative agreements that have been concluded which support and enable the production and trade of DCF commodities
Number of targeted companies and financial institutions with changed policies, practices and/or public reactions (Core Indicator 9)
Evidence of increased leadership, influence, and concrete benefits for women and under-represented groups in the development, adoption, and application of deforestation- and conversion-free (DCF) standards</narrative>
  </description>
